<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugo c.bank keeps short-term bond rate unchanged.</title>
<headline>Yugo c.bank keeps short-term bond rate unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Yugoslavia (NBY) left the interest rate on its short-term bonds auctioned on Monday unchanged at a monthly three percent, the Belgrade bourse said.</p>
<p>The three percent monthly rate, corresponding to an annual 41.63 percent, was kept unchanged since mid-May.</p>
<p>The NBY offered for sale a new 100-million dinar ($16.4 million) tranche of 30-day bonds, issued at a 10,000 dinar face value, but sold only 0.5 million dinars worth, the bourse said.</p>
<p>-- Gordana Filipovic, Belgrade newsroom, +381 11 311 4254</p>
<p>($1 = 6.0878 Yugoslav dinars)</p>
